From: programista-zacny <5969291+programista-zacny@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shmem: honour MFD_ALLOW_SEALING and finish the sealing checks

memfd_create(name, MFD_ALLOW_SEALING) returned a file that could not be
sealed: every fcntl(fd, F_ADD_SEALS, ...) failed with EPERM, whatever
seals were asked for. shmem_get_inode() starts every inode with
F_SEAL_SEAL set, and shmem_add_seals() returns -EPERM as long as that bit
is set. Upstream clears it in memfd_create() when MFD_ALLOW_SEALING is
given; the backport of memfd_create() in this tree was taken before the
sealing API existed in it, so those two lines were dropped and never came
back ("info" was assigned there but not used).

On the device this made zygote log
  fcntl(F_ADD_SEALS) failed: Operation not permitted, no memfd support.
on every boot, fall back to ashmem for the zygote JIT cache, and give up
on sharing the boot image methods between zygote and its children
("Failed to seal boot image methods file descriptor").

While here, bring the rest of the sealing code in line with upstream so
that seals which can now be set are also enforced:
- FALLOC_FL_PUNCH_HOLE has to be refused on a write-sealed file. The
  check was missing, so a file sealed with F_SEAL_WRITE or
  F_SEAL_FUTURE_WRITE could still be zeroed through fallocate().
- F_SEAL_FUTURE_WRITE cleared VM_MAYWRITE on private mappings too, which
  makes mprotect(PROT_WRITE) of a MAP_PRIVATE mapping fail. Only shared
  mappings need it.

Derived from upstream:
  9183df25fe7b "shm: add memfd_create() syscall"         (the two lines
               in memfd_create())
  40e041a2c858 "shm: add sealing API"                    (punch-hole check)
  ab3948f58ff8 "mm/memfd: add an F_SEAL_FUTURE_WRITE seal to memfd"
               (punch-hole check covers the future-write seal)
  05d351102dbe "mm, memfd: fix COW issue on MAP_PRIVATE and
               F_SEAL_FUTURE_WRITE mappings"

Adapted for 3.10: the sealing code lives in mm/shmem.c here (upstream
moved it to mm/memfd.c in 4.16). Nothing else changes; the i_mmap_writable
accounting that F_SEAL_WRITE relies on (4bb5f5d9395b) and
shmem_wait_for_pins() are already in the tree.

Not compile-tested.
---
 mm/shmem.c | 19 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mm/shmem.c b/mm/shmem.c
index af9a963..7b94062 100644
--- a/mm/shmem.c
+++ b/mm/shmem.c
@@ -1443,11 +1443,14 @@ static int shmem_mmap(struct file *file, struct vm_area_struct *vma)
 			return -EPERM;
 
 		/*
-		 * Since the F_SEAL_FUTURE_WRITE seals allow for a MAP_SHARED
-		 * read-only mapping, take care to not allow mprotect to revert
-		 * protections.
+		 * Since an F_SEAL_FUTURE_WRITE sealed memfd can be mapped as
+		 * MAP_SHARED and read-only, take care to not allow mprotect to
+		 * revert protections on such mappings. Do this only for shared
+		 * mappings. For private mappings, don't need to mask
+		 * VM_MAYWRITE as we still want them to be COW-writable.
 		 */
-		vma->vm_flags &= ~(VM_MAYWRITE);
+		if (vma->vm_flags & VM_SHARED)
+			vma->vm_flags &= ~(VM_MAYWRITE);
 	}
 
 	file_accessed(file);
@@ -2162,6 +2165,12 @@ static long shmem_fallocate(struct file *file, int mode, loff_t offset,
 		loff_t unmap_end = round_down(offset + len, PAGE_SIZE) - 1;
 		DECLARE_WAIT_QUEUE_HEAD_ONSTACK(shmem_falloc_waitq);
 
+		/* protected by i_mutex */
+		if (info->seals & (F_SEAL_WRITE | F_SEAL_FUTURE_WRITE)) {
+			error = -EPERM;
+			goto out;
+		}
+
 		shmem_falloc.waitq = &shmem_falloc_waitq;
 		shmem_falloc.start = unmap_start >> PAGE_SHIFT;
 		shmem_falloc.next = (unmap_end + 1) >> PAGE_SHIFT;
@@ -2970,6 +2979,8 @@ SYSCALL_DEFINE2(memfd_create,
 	info = SHMEM_I(file->f_path.dentry->d_inode);
 	file->f_mode |= FMODE_LSEEK | FMODE_PREAD | FMODE_PWRITE;
 	file->f_flags |= O_RDWR | O_LARGEFILE;
+	if (flags & MFD_ALLOW_SEALING)
+		info->seals &= ~F_SEAL_SEAL;
 
 	fd_install(fd, file);
 	kfree(name);
